          "sourceRegion": "Shared answer graph beneath part b",
          "description": "Editable graph shared by parts b and c. Horizontal ticks run from −2 to 7 and vertical ticks from −1 to 7. Axes use the requested ride variables W and F. Solid boundaries enclose the non-negative feasible region with F capped at 6. Light blue shading marks unwanted regions; blue crosses mark all 24 feasible integer points.",
          "mathematics": "0≤W≤5, 0≤F≤6, 4W+3F≤20. Cost boundary F=(20−4W)/3 has intercepts (0,20/3) and (5,0). Feasible polygon: (0,0),(5,0),(1/2,6),(0,6). Integer columns contain 7,6,5,3,2,1 points respectively for W=0,1,2,3,4,5.",
